.TH INVF-STATS 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf\-stats \- InvariantFS volume statistics and zone overview
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf\-stats
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.IR image | device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf\-stats
opens an unmounted InvariantFS volume and prints a human-readable summary of
its population, zone layout, compression ratios, and (for two-device volumes)
tier/mirror status.
.PP
The volume must not be actively mounted by
.BR invf\-fuse (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
The output includes:
.IP \(bu 2
Volume state
.RB ( CLEAN " or " DIRTY )
and capacity (total blocks \(mu 4 KiB).
.IP \(bu 2
Zone sizes: metadata, RAW, shadow (in MiB).
.IP \(bu 2
Used/free space.
.IP \(bu 2
Population: files, directories, symlinks, special nodes, tombstones, bad
records.
.IP \(bu 2
Data statistics: logical bytes, biggest file, estimated compression ratio.
.IP \(bu 2
Per-zone detail with logical/physical sizes and ratios (RAW, SHADOW, TEXT,
unclaimed).
.IP \(bu 2
Two-device (WP25) info when applicable: device count, mirror status, raw
mirror segments, tier copies.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on open or walk errors; 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf\-fuse (8),
.BR invf\-sweep (8),
.BR invf\-verify (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
